    "finalText": "Both suites pass. The work is complete — here's the summary.\n\n## What was broken (against `docs/CONTRACT.md`)\n\n1. **Tenant isolation** — `src/storage.js:1` keyed rows by `id` alone, so equal ids in different tenants overwrote each other.\n2. **Replay lost deletions** — `src/replay.js:1` filtered to `op === 'put'`, so `open(exportJournal())` resurrected every deleted pair.\n3. **`batch` ignored the event op** — `src/api.js:15` always did `rows.set(...)`, so a `{op:'delete'}` event in a batch never deleted anything (and bypassed the shared apply path).\n4. **Stale cache on every mutation path** — `get` cached both hits and misses, but `put`/`remove`/`batch` never invalidated, so cached values (including cached misses) went stale after any mutation.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- `src/storage.js` — key is now `JSON.stringify([tenant, id])`: collision-free for arbitrary strings, including ones containing delimiter characters.\n- `src/replay.js` — replays both `put` and `delete` events, in order.\n- `src/api.js` —\n  - `apply()` now deletes the affected cache key, so every mutation path (`put`, `remove`, `batch`, and replay during `open`) keeps reads fresh;\n  - `batch` routes each event through `mutate`, so ops are honored, applied in call order, and journaled.\n\n`exportJournal` detachment and journal seeding from `history` already satisfied the contract and were left intact.\n\n## Tests added\n\n`run-tests.js` went from a 1-case smoke test to 11 cases, one per contract obligation: call order, cached-hit and cached-miss freshness on each mutation path, batch deletes, tenant independence, delimiter-collision keys, export detachment (mutate the result → state and later exports unaffected), journal order/ops, history input not aliased, full replay equivalence including deletions, and repeated replay staying equivalent. The sealed check `checks/contract.cjs` and `amabie.project.json` were left untouched.\n\n**Current status:** `node run-tests.js` → `11 passing`; `node checks/contract.cjs` → `contract checks passed`."
